WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.200
A flattened table is a bag of numbers.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.200
Which plan costs forty-nine?

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.700
So keep the tables and the headings.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.500
The heading says which plan it is about.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.000
And skip pages with nothing on them.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.900
The first threshold rejected a real page.

7
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.000
Then run every piece in order.

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.100
Each one says what it decided.

9
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.400
The first real run did not work.

10
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.300
A page showing two prices. It found none.

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.800
Six things could be wrong. One was.

12
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.500
Same words. Fewer of them. It answers.

13
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.200
We wrote this down before it happened.

14
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.300
The set measures what the pipeline does not.

15
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.700
So the next piece is not optional.

16
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.900
Failing here is cheaper than shipping it.
